  <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Common Error</th><th>Correction</th></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Arms too high (above heart)</td><td>Lower to heart height — too high causes shoulder tension</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Arms too low</td><td>Raise to heart height — too low causes back tension</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Arms straightened</td><td>Maintain a natural rounded arc</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Shrugging shoulders</td><td>Sink shoulders, drop elbows; armpit balloon imagery</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Hands too close or too far apart</td><td>Imagine holding a balloon — don't squeeze it or let it drop</td></tr>
  </table>

  ---

  <h2>Quick Reference Card</h2>
  <div class="cheatsheet">
    <h4>🫂 Holding the Balloon — One-Page Quick Reference</h4>
    <dl>
      <dt>Feet/Knees/Body</dt><dd>Same as Wu Chi: shoulder-width, slightly bent, sitting-not-sitting</dd>
      <dt>Hand position</dt><dd>Heart height, round embrace as if holding a balloon</dd>
      <dt>Distance</dt><dd>Don't squeeze (too close) or drop (too far)</dd>
      <dt>Arm shape</dt><dd>Natural rounded arc, not straightened</dd>
      <dt>Fingers</dt><dd>Slightly spread, as if touching a marble at each fingertip</dd>
      <dt>Mental focus</dt><dd>Armpit balloons + balloon chair + head suspended</dd>
      <dt>Duration</dt><dd>Start with 3-5 minutes, gradually increase to 20 minutes</dd>
      <dt>Flow</dt><dd>Warm-up (Holding Up the Sky / Drawing the Bow) → Holding the Balloon → Cool-down</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

